WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.105
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:10.612
Last time we built the map.

5
00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:16.363
Today we open the Advanced folder underneath it: the notes Voyage uses when it makes up places for you,

6
00:00:16.363 --> 00:00:18.317
and the settings for the whole map.

7
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.763
Open Map, then Advanced, then Region Archetypes.

8
00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:26.676
Every new world comes with twenty-three of these, ready to go.

9
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.821
Each one is a name and one box of notes.

10
00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:35.263
Frontier has geography, dynamics, history and atmosphere, a few short lines each.

11
00:00:35.263 --> 00:00:39.765
It's the feel Voyage reaches for when it makes up a region for you.

12
00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.589
Location Archetypes are the same idea for places.

13
00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:49.549
Eleven come with every world, and I've added one of ours at the bottom.

14
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.343
Show Comes to Town.

15
00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:55.546
Atmosphere, tensions, patterns and secrets, three lines each.

16
00:00:55.546 --> 00:01:00.715
Name it after a situation, not a kind of place: Power Struggle, not Forest.

17
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.543
So when do they matter?

18
00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:07.807
When Voyage makes up a place for you, like a new region during play,

19
00:01:07.807 --> 00:01:10.755
or the details of a location you left on Basic.

20
00:01:10.755 --> 00:01:13.954
Anything you wrote as Detailed uses your own words.

21
00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:18.982
Last one in the folder, Location Settings.

22
00:01:18.982 --> 00:01:25.781
New region generation lets the story add new regions during play. It starts on.

23
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:30.179
Encounters switches on Voyage's random encounters.

24
00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:31.284
It starts off.

25
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:35.955
Border feathering fades the edges of each region's map picture.

26
00:01:35.955 --> 00:01:38.100
Studio worlds start with it off.

27
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.925
Leave it off if you want your region pictures to line up as one big map.

28
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:48.490
Region size is how wide each square is in kilometres, a hundred to start.

29
00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:52.701
Simple and complex radius are how big each kind of place is.

30
00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:57.372
Location count is how many places Voyage puts in a region it makes up,

31
00:01:57.372 --> 00:02:00.255
then the average and shortest trip between them.

32
00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:04.219
Voyage's own advice: keep the defaults unless you've got a reason.

33
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:07.241
That's the map folder done.

34
00:02:07.241 --> 00:02:09.801
Our archetype is linked in the description.

35
00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:13.670
Next time, the page you fill in before you draw a single picture,

36
00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.825
your world's art style, and then we'll draw that map.

37
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:21.215
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

